# Copy this file to `.private-names` (which is gitignored and must never be
# committed). One protected string per line. Lines starting with # are
# comments; blank lines are ignored. Matching is case-insensitive on word
# boundaries.
#
# Put here every string that must never appear in a tracked file:
#   - your real first and last name
#   - the local-part of your personal email (the bit before the @)
#   - your machine's username / home-folder name
#   - your machine's hostname, if distinctive
#   - real first names of players, friends, or anyone else in your orbit
#
# The scanners report a masked form ("Jo…", 6 chars) — never the string
# itself — so a finding can be acted on without republishing the thing it
# found.
#
# Example entries (replace with your own):
#Jordan
#jordan.surname
#JORDANS-DESKTOP
